✔ asset update stores SD2 identity declaration as a SQLite integer and returns a boolean (16.233ms)
✔ asset update serializes metadata and tags before binding them to SQLite (4.8336ms)
✔ asset checksum lookup deduplicates only within the same asset scope (3.8349ms)
✔ personal media checksum lookup never returns another user's asset (2.7402ms)
✔ asset lineage retains ancestors and derived versions, including soft-deleted entries (3.8251ms)
✔ locally archived media never exposes a supplier signed URL (1.7572ms)
✔ asset lookup by id uses the same personal/project scope as the library (2.9884ms)
✔ project owner retains CRUD access when a legacy asset has a stale direct owner (12.0296ms)
✔ new assets receive a stable type-prefixed reference alias while retaining the original file name (3.2305ms)
✔ deleting an asset automatically removes editable storyboard and free-create references (13.547ms)
✔ archiving a project asset hides it from new library selection without changing editable shot references (13.2632ms)
✔ bulk asset deletion is scoped to the current user and includes their project assets (4.266ms)
✔ SD2 batch queue only marks the caller-owned image assets (3.8724ms)
✔ omni video rejects material counts above the per-shot media limits (4.7442ms)
✔ prompt-reference selection permits text-only video and keeps frame inputs (0.9335ms)
✔ global and project asset scopes are isolated for the same owner (4.3449ms)
✔ asset search finds reference aliases beyond the first page without crossing owners (13.1484ms)
✔ Seedance 2.5 applies its model-specific reference limits instead of legacy model limits (14.0992ms)
✔ first-last-frame mode accepts a first frame without an optional tail frame (1.0973ms)
✔ Seedance rejects declared real-person material without an active certification (2.1993ms)
✔ Seedance treats every Richbest in-progress stage as a wait state (1.7825ms)
✔ Seedance uses active remote library references for every supported media type (1.5797ms)
✔ omni job API snapshot masks local and remote source URLs (1.1157ms)
✔ video capabilities only advertise native media modes with an adapter (1.4123ms)
✔ only Seedance 2.5 generation settings allow durations above 15 seconds (5.6399ms)
✔ Seedance 2.5 duration survives a storyboard-only override (33.7211ms)
✔ free-create shot stores independent model, duration and resolution (16.8618ms)
✔ new free-create shots default to 15 seconds (5.9124ms)
✔ classic storyboard persists per-shot text and video generation settings (10.1145ms)
✔ first storyboard edit establishes episode defaults, later edits only override the current shot (7.6798ms)
✔ storyboard master defaults to 1080p enhancement without interpolation and synchronizes explicit changes (7.9029ms)
✔ a later storyboard edited before settings are loaded becomes an override and never redefines the first-shot master (6.0101ms)
✔ generation master follows the same visual sort and duplicate-shot dedupe as the storyboard list (2.3817ms)
✔ episode merge ignores storyboard image local_path when selecting a video URL (4.5106ms)
✔ episode merge uses the adopted version and never falls back when it is failed (3.334ms)
✔ price queries read all models in signed pages of twenty (11.2368ms)
✔ upstream price timeouts reduce page size and restart without mixing snapshots (525.4988ms)
✔ read-only price queries retry upstream timeouts but not authentication errors (267.7358ms)
✔ aborted reads return a bounded timeout; failed pagination retains earlier request IDs (260.7862ms)
